Derived, with modification
--------------------------

  src/Buffer.php
      The consumer-strategy split, the chunking of a large payload into several
      requests, and the retry loop follow mixpanel-php's ConsumerStrategies.

      Changed: the retry policy is Intempt's. A 413 halves the batch width and
      recovers by doubling after ten full-width successes; 429 honours
      Retry-After; a circuit breaker opens after five consecutive failures; and
      a close-initiated drain is bounded. mixpanel-php retries on a fixed
      schedule with no width adaptation and no breaker.

  src/Transport.php
      The curl consumer and the response error mapping follow mixpanel-php's
      CurlConsumer.

      Changed: adds a per-request timeout, distinguishes retryable from
      non-retryable status codes, keeps credentials out of every error surface,
      and never coerces a platform id numerically.

  src/Validate.php
      timestamp() follows mixpanel-php's timestamp normalisation.
      chunk() follows its batching helper.

      Changed: chunk() rejects a size below one rather than looping forever;
      timestamp() rejects non-finite input instead of coercing it.

Not derived
-----------

Everything else is original: the Intempt wire format, the identity model
(userId and accountId only), consent, commerce, feed recommendations, the
opt-out gate, configuration handling and the whole test suite.

